      "content": "**Why jobs can retry forever:**\n\nIn `worker.ts`, the retry logic is:\n\n```ts\nif (config.maxRetries === 0 || job.attempts < config.maxRetries) return enqueue(job);\n```\n\nThe condition `config.maxRetries === 0` short-circuits to `true`, so when `maxRetries` is `0`, the job is **always re-enqueued** regardless of how many attempts it has already made. The comment in the file confirms the intent: *\"maxRetries=0 explicitly means unlimited retries.\"*\n\nIn `config.json`, `\"maxRetries\": 0` is set, which triggers this unlimited-retry path.\n\n**Correction:**\n\nChange `config.json` from `\"maxRetries\": 0` to a finite positive value, e.g. `\"maxRetries\": 3`, so that after 3 failed attempts the job is routed to the dead-letter queue instead of being re-enqueued indefinitely.",
